ows found in the montane life zone to glistening alpine lakes and up to the towering mountain peaks, there is something for everyone to discover. Along the way explore over 300 miles of hiking trails and incredible wildlife viewing.","full_name":"Rocky Mountain National Park","hash_scope":"normalized_record","id":"67A56B17-F533-4A56-B2DA-26091C6AD295","observed_changed_at":"2026-10-03T03:45:48.554581Z","observed_first_at":"2026-10-03T03:45:48.554581Z","park_code":"romo","seasonal_weather":{"kind":"seasonal_context","text":"Weather can change quickly in Rocky Mountain National Park due to the mountains and elevation. Elevation in the park ranges from 7,800 feet above sea level to over 14,000 feet at the top of the tallest mountain peaks. Weather conditions can change quickly throughout the day. For detailed weather information, visit https://www.nps.gov/romo/planyourvisit/all-about-weather.htm For the most up-to-date weather forecasts, visit the National Weather Service webpage for Rocky at https://www.weather.gov/bou/rmnp"},"source_updated_at":null,"url":"https://www.nps.gov/romo/index.htm"},"provider":"NPS","published_at":null,"schema_version":1,"source_issued_at":null,"source_updated_at":null,"source_url":"https://developer.nps.gov/api/v1/parks?parkCode=romo"},{"collection_status":"success","coverage_status":"checked_profile_only","error_code":null,"last_checked_at":"2026-10-03T03:45:48.554581Z","last_successful_fetch_at":"2026-10-03T03:45:48.554581Z","park_code":"yell","profile":{"activity_categories":[{"id":"01D717BC-18BB-4FE4-95BA-6B13AD702038","name":"Snowshoeing"},{"id":"0307955A-B65C-4CE4-A780-EB36BAAADF0B","name":"Horse Trekking"},{"id":"071BA73C-1D3C-46D4-A53C-00D5602F7F0E","name":"Boating"},{"id":"09DF0950-D319-4557-A57E-04CD2F63FF42","name":"Arts and Culture"},{"id":"0B4A5320-216D-451A-9990-626E1D5ACE28","name":"Scenic Driving"},{"id":"0B685688-3405-4E2A-ABBA-E3069492EC50","name":"Wildlife Watching"},{"id":"0C0D142F-06B5-4BE1-8B44-491B90F93DEB","name":"P