ions, including a warm jacket and rain gear, even in the summer."},"source_updated_at":null,"url":"https://www.nps.gov/yell/index.htm"},"provider":"NPS","published_at":null,"schema_version":1,"source_issued_at":null,"source_updated_at":null,"source_url":"https://developer.nps.gov/api/v1/parks?parkCode=yell"},{"collection_status":"success","coverage_status":"checked_profile_only","error_code":null,"last_checked_at":"2026-10-03T03:45:48.554581Z","last_successful_fetch_at":"2026-10-03T03:45:48.554581Z","park_code":"zion","profile":{"activity_categories":[{"id":"07CBCA6A-46B8-413F-8B6C-ABEDEBF9853E","name":"Canyoneering"},{"id":"09DF0950-D319-4557-A57E-04CD2F63FF42","name":"Arts and Culture"},{"id":"0B685688-3405-4E2A-ABBA-E3069492EC50","name":"Wildlife Watching"},{"id":"0C0D142F-06B5-4BE1-8B44-491B90F93DEB","name":"Park Film"},{"id":"13A57703-BB1A-41A2-94B8-53B692EB7238","name":"Astronomy"},{"id":"24380E3F-AD9D-4E38-BF13-C8EEB21893E7","name":"Shopping"},{"id":"45261C0A-00D8-4C27-A1F8-029F933A0D34","name":"Front-Country Hiking"},{"id":"467DC8B8-0B7D-436D-A026-80A22358F615","name":"Bookstore and Park Store"},{"id":"4A58AF13-E8FB-4530-B41A-97DF0B0C77B7","name":"Backcountry Camping"},{"id":"5A2C91D1-50EC-4B24-8BED-A2E11A1892DF","name":"Birdwatching"},{"id":"7CE6E935-F839-4FEC-A63E-052B1DEF39D2","name":"Biking"},{"id":"80229F2D-972E-40A8-8860-232551CC30D6","name":"Horse Camping (see also Horse/Stock Use)"},{"id":"87D3B1CD-3903-4561-ABB1-2DD870C43F2F","name":"Rock Climbing"},{"id":"8D778629-F603-4C50-A121-6F4BB2FE2C4B","name":"Road Biking"},{"id":"9159DF0F-951D-4AAE-9987-CEB3CE2A9ADA","name":"Car or Front Country Camping"},{"id":"A59947B7-3376-49B4-AD02-C0423E08C5F7","name":"Camping"},{"id":"B12FAAB9-713F-4B38-83E4-A273F5A43C77","name":"Climbing"},{"id":"B33DC9B6-0B7D-4322-BAD7-A13A34C584A3","name":"Guided Tours"},{"id":"BFF8C027-7C8F-480B-A5F8-CD8CE490BFBA","name":"Hiking"},{"id":"C8F98B28-3C10-41AE-AA99-092B3B398C43","name":"Museum Exhibits"},{"id":"D37A0003-8317-4F04-8FB0-4CF0A272E195","name":"Stargazing"},{"id":"DF4A35E0-7983-4A3E-BC47-F37B872B0F25","name":"Junior Ranger Program"}],"activity_scope":"categories_only","content_hash":"f1471b3d5f80d62bcb334175a6f19347371f4e6be73326d39b8eb21f464a522c","description":"Follow the paths where people have walked for thousands of years. Gaze up at massive sandstone cliffs of cream, pink, and red that soar into a brilliant blue sky. Experience the tall, stretching walls of a narrow slot canyon. Zion’s unique array of plants and animals will enchant you as you absorb the rich history of the past and enjoy the excitement of present-day adventures.","full_name":"Zion National Park","hash_scope":"normalized_record","id":"41BAB8ED-C95F-447D-9DA1-FCC4E4D808B2","observed_changed_at":"2026-10-03T03:45:48.554581Z","observed_first_at":"2026-10-03T03:45:48.554581Z","park_code":"zion","seasonal_weather":{"kind":"seasonal_context","text":"Zion is known for a wide range of weather conditions. Temperatures vary with changes in elevation and day/night temperatures may differ by over 30°F (16°C). In summer, temperatures in Zion National Park often exceed 100°F (38°C). Zion experiences monsoons from mid-July into September that result in an increased risk of flash floods. Always be aware of the threat of storms and lightning and be prepared for a wide range of weather conditions. Winters are generally mild."},"source_updated_at":null,"url":"https://www.nps.gov/zion/index.htm"},"provider":"NPS","published_at":null,"schema_version":1,"source_issued_at":null,"source_updated_at":null,"source_url":"https://developer.nps.gov/api/v1/parks?parkCode=zion"},{"collection_status":"success","coverage_status":"checked_profile_only","error_code":null,"last_checked_at":"2026-10-03T03:45:48.554581Z","last_successful_fetch_at":"2026-10-03T03:45:48.554581Z","park_code":"grca","profile":{"activity_categories":[{"id":"0307955A-B65C-4CE4-A780-EB36BAAADF0B","name":"Horse Trekking"},{"id":"071BA73C-1D3C-46D4-A53C-00D5602F7F0E","name":